":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-28T16:26:17Z","updated_at":"2025-04-28T16:26:17Z","body":"Note, `@static_unload` does not work as a workaround.  It may be due to me using a more complex case of statics defined within a class declared in a file as follows, but the statics did not update when hot-reloading, even with `@static_unload` set in the source file.  Renaming the variable did work though.\n\n```gdscript\n@tool\n@static_unload\nextends SubViewportContaner\n\n@export ....\n\nclass HexCell:\n    extends Node3D\n    static var dict = {}\n    static func _static_init() -> void:\n        dict[\"key\"] = calculated_value_i_need_to_update\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2835814759/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]